&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working at Tech Holding isn&#39;t just a job, it&#39;s an opportunity to be a part of something bigger. We are a full-service consulting firm that was founded on the premise of delivering predictable outcomes and high-quality solutions to our clients.&amp;nbsp; Our founders and team members have industry experience and have held senior positions in a wide variety of companies – from emerging startups to large Fortune 50 firms – and we have taken our combined experiences and developed a unique approach that is supported by the principles of deep expertise, integrity, transparency, and dependability.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;product designer with an exceptional craft bar&lt;/strong&gt; to help shape a complex software product.&lt;br&gt;The hard part of this role isn’t handling complexity — it’s making complexity disappear. We want someone who can take a genuinely thorny problem space and ship something that feels obvious, fast, and well-made. Think the way a Ramp, Linear, or Attio treats an equally complicated domain.&lt;br&gt;This is a product design role, not a traditional enterprise UX role. If your instinct is to start with a requirements doc and a stakeholder matrix, this isn’t the fit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape product direction alongside product and engineering — not wait to be handed specs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype fast and often; put something in front of people in days, not sprints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design core surfaces end to end, with real interaction depth — empty states, loading, errors, keyboard behavior, motion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a strong point of view on craft and hold the quality bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish the visual and systemic foundation the product grows on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate with ambiguity: figure out what’s needed, then go build it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Craft and taste, first.&lt;/strong&gt; Your portfolio should make us want to use the thing. We’re looking for evidence you’ve made something complicated feel simple — clear hierarchy, considered interaction detail, restraint. Show us the polish.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product design instincts.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ve shaped direction, not just executed tickets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Startup pace.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ve worked somewhere small and fast, where the answer wasn’t known in advance and you figured it out by building.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Depth on complex interfaces.&lt;/strong&gt; Data-dense views, filtering, multi-step flows, role-based experiences — ideally in a product where users were demanding and the UI still felt great.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expert Figma&lt;/strong&gt;, high-fidelity prototyping, and the ability to defend design decisions to non-designers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Front-end fluency or coded prototyping&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design systems built for scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record at a venture-backed product company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4 data-start=&quot;290&quot; data-end=&quot;312&quot;&gt;What We’re&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;Not&lt;/em&gt; Optimizing For&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We’d rather get the caliber and type of designer right than match industry background.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain or industry experience is &lt;strong&gt;not&lt;/strong&gt; required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Years of experience is &lt;strong&gt;not&lt;/strong&gt; a filter — a five-year designer with an outstanding portfolio beats a fifteen-year designer with a process deck&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep enterprise or Fortune 500 UX tenure is &lt;strong&gt;not&lt;/strong&gt; an advantage, and can be a liability if it came with heavy process and a low visual bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4 data-start=&quot;290&quot; data-end=&quot;312&quot;&gt;Employment type:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contract&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully remote in the USA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
