&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Tech Holding is proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds and experiences, and we consider qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristic. If you require accommodation in the application process, please contact our HR&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working at Tech Holding isn&#39;t just a job, it&#39;s an opportunity to be a part of something bigger. We are a full-service consulting firm that was founded on the premise of delivering predictable outcomes and high-quality solutions to our clients.&amp;nbsp; Our founders and team members have industry experience and have held senior positions in a wide variety of companies – from emerging startups to large Fortune 50 firms – and we have taken our combined experiences and developed a unique approach that is supported by the principles of deep expertise, integrity, transparency, and dependability.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior SDET / Test Automation Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; for a project based assignment to build the automated testing and release systems that ensure our products remain reliable as traffic, data volume, integrations, partners, and release velocity increase.&amp;nbsp;This is a hands-on engineering role focused on &lt;strong&gt;test automation, API and integration testing, performance and scalability testing, and CI/CD quality gates&lt;/strong&gt; within an AWS-based environment.&lt;br&gt;This is not a manual QA position. You will design and build reusable test infrastructure, automate critical product and partner workflows, create realistic performance scenarios, and provide engineering teams with clear evidence of whether a release is ready for production.&lt;br&gt;You will work closely with engineering teams and the Performance &amp;amp; Reliability Engineering Lead to ensure quality and scalability are built into the development lifecycle rather than treated as a final release checkpoint.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and evolve the automated testing architecture across products and engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain automated &lt;strong&gt;API, integration, contract, end-to-end, regression, and UI tests where appropriate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop reusable test frameworks, fixtures, synthetic data, mocks, and environment strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build automated testing for distributed services and integrations running within &lt;strong&gt;AWS environments&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and execute &lt;strong&gt;load, stress, spike, soak, scalability, degradation, and recovery tests&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate performance and capacity scenarios into repeatable automated test suites with measurable pass/fail thresholds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Model realistic workloads, concurrency levels, traffic patterns, data volumes, and dependency behavior&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate automated suites into CI/CD pipelines and establish enforceable quality and release gates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create automated release checks tied to quality, latency, reliability, and performance thresholds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish practices for identifying, quarantining, diagnosing, and eliminating flaky tests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve test observability and failure reporting so engineers can quickly understand and diagnose issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain reliable test data and test environment strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debug failures across APIs, services, databases, infrastructure, and external integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Performance &amp;amp; Reliability Engineering to validate scalability assumptions and production readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Security Engineering on permissions, isolation, negative-path, and abuse-related test scenarios&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track testing trends and help reduce escaped defects, flaky tests, manual release effort, and regression risk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach engineers on testability, automation, quality ownership, and defect-prevention practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience as an &lt;strong&gt;SDET, Software Engineer in Test, Test Automation Engineer, Quality Engineer, or similar engineering-focused testing role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong software development and test automation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience testing &lt;strong&gt;APIs, distributed services, integrations, and cloud-based applications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience working within &lt;strong&gt;AWS environments&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience building automated API and integration test frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on performance and scalability testing experience using tools such as &lt;strong&gt;k6, Gatling, Locust, JMeter, or equivalent&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing realistic performance workloads rather than simply executing predefined load tests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with &lt;strong&gt;load, stress, spike, soak, and scalability testing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience integrating automated tests into &lt;strong&gt;CI/CD pipelines&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience establishing automated quality gates and release criteria&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with contract testing and testing across service boundaries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of test-data management, synthetic data, fixtures, mocks, and environment reliability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using logs, metrics, traces, and other observability tools to diagnose test and system failures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong debugging skills across applications, APIs, infrastructure, databases, and integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience identifying and reducing flaky or unreliable automated tests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence engineering teams and promote shared ownership of quality without becoming a centralized testing bottleneck&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience testing high-scale SaaS or distributed platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AWS services supporting highly available or distributed applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience testing systems with significant traffic, concurrency, or availability requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with resilience, failure injection, dependency degradation, or recovery testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with infrastructure-as-code and ephemeral or automated test environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with security-adjacent testing, including permissions, authentication, authorization, isolation, and negative-path scenarios&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identity, DNS, registry, or security domain experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building quality or test platforms used across multiple engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4 data-start=&quot;290&quot; data-end=&quot;312&quot;&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;br&gt;Within your first several months, you will have:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established a clear risk-based automation strategy across critical product and partner workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built reliable automated regression, API, integration, and contract test coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Created repeatable performance and scalability tests for the platform&#39;s highest-risk journeys&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established realistic test-data and environment strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrated critical test suites directly into CI/CD pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implemented measurable release gates tied to quality, latency, reliability, and performance thresholds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduced flaky tests and improved the clarity and actionability of automated test failures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established performance trend reporting and repeatable load, soak, and failure-testing capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduced manual release validation and increased confidence in production readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Helped establish shared quality ownership across engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
