&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working at Tech Holding isn&#39;t just a job, it&#39;s an opportunity to be a part of something bigger. We are a full-service consulting firm that was founded on the premise of delivering predictable outcomes and high-quality solutions to our clients.&amp;nbsp; Our founders and team members have industry experience and have held senior positions in a wide variety of companies – from emerging startups to large Fortune 50 firms – and we have taken our combined experiences and developed a unique approach that is supported by the principles of deep expertise, integrity, transparency, and dependability.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Technical Customer Success &amp;amp; Deployment Lead&lt;/strong&gt; for a project based assignment to turn committed pilots and customer deployments into successful implementations, measurable adoption, and long-term product value.&lt;br&gt;This is a customer-facing, enterprise-oriented role that sits at the intersection of customer success, implementation, technical delivery, product, and engineering.&lt;br&gt;You will own the operating relationship once an opportunity becomes a committed pilot or deployment. That includes onboarding, readiness, implementation planning, stakeholder coordination, adoption, issue triage, escalations, and ensuring customer feedback makes its way back into the product organization.&lt;br&gt;This is not a traditional support role or a quota-carrying sales position. You will be responsible for creating structure around complex customer deployments while protecting engineering teams from fragmented or unmanaged customer requests.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the customer operating cadence from pilot kickoff through deployment, adoption, and final pilot decision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage implementation plans, readiness checklists, milestones, dependencies, success criteria, and ownership matrices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead customer kickoffs and recurring deployment and status meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate dependencies across customers, GTM, Product, Partner Engineering, Security, Legal, and engineering delivery teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure each deployment has clear owners, timelines, risks, escalation paths, and measurable success criteria&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track customer usage, adoption, product health, risks, decisions, commitments, incidents, and follow-up actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Surface blockers early and drive accountability across internal and external stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triage customer issues into the appropriate category, including support, configuration, integration, product defect, roadmap request, or commercial discussion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Route technical and product issues to the correct internal owner with clear context and supporting information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own customer-facing status updates and escalation communications during deployments and operational incidents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help customers understand the distinction between existing product capabilities, configuration, integration work, and future roadmap items&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capture structured customer feedback and ensure Product and Engineering close the loop on decisions and learnings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor customer health and adoption signals and identify risks to successful deployment or expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop reusable onboarding guides, implementation playbooks, runbooks, training materials, FAQs, and customer handoff processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive pilots toward a clear outcome, including expand, convert, continue learning, pause, or exit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience in &lt;strong&gt;enterprise technical customer success, implementation, solutions delivery, technical program management, or a similar customer-facing technical role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with &lt;strong&gt;platform, SaaS, API-driven, integration-heavy, or technical enterprise products&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading complex customer implementations or deployments from kickoff through production adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to coordinate business, executive, product, engineering, security, and technical stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating and managing implementation plans, milestones, dependencies, risks, ownership models, and escalation processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical fluency with APIs, integrations, environments, system dependencies, and common software delivery concepts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand and communicate technical issues without needing to be the engineer implementing the solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong issue-triage skills and the ability to distinguish between configuration problems, integration issues, product defects, roadmap requests, and commercial concerns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing customer escalations and communicating clearly during high-pressure delivery or operational situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, particularly with enterprise customers and senior stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to turn ambiguous customer requests into structured, actionable information for Product and Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational discipline and attention to detail across multiple simultaneous customer commitments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working in an early-stage or rapidly evolving environment where implementation and customer-success processes are still being developed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting identity, security, infrastructure, DNS, registry, or other technically complex platform products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with enterprise API integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting customer pilots, proofs of concept, or phased production rollouts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with customer health metrics, adoption reporting, and implementation analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with solutions engineering, product management, and engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building customer onboarding or implementation processes from the ground up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with security, compliance, and enterprise procurement processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting strategic enterprise customers with complex organizational structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4 data-start=&quot;290&quot; data-end=&quot;312&quot;&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;br&gt;Within your first several months, you will have:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established a repeatable pilot and deployment process with clear plans, ownership, milestones, risks, and escalation paths&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Created standardized kickoff, readiness, RACI, success-measurement, and deployment templates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Brought visibility to active deployments, adoption, risks, issues, and customer health&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established a consistent operating cadence for priority customers and pilots&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improved the quality and structure of issues routed to Product and Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduced fragmented customer requests and unnecessary interruptions to engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Created reusable onboarding, training, handoff, and deployment materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established a structured customer-feedback loop into Product and Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Helped customers reach first value more predictably&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensured pilots conclude with clear evidence and an explicit decision on whether to expand, convert, continue learning, pause, or exit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
